prompt:
A real photograph, taken with a good phone camera and looking exactly like a phone photograph, of a small office in a Bürgeramt, the citizens' registration office of a Berlin district, on a weekday morning, taken as a person waiting by the door a few metres away would take it, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, white ceiling lights and grey daylight from a window at the back. The textures of real laminate desk, paper, plastic, metal, fabric and skin, with the true depth and the slight lens perspective of a photograph.

The first reference picture shows the young man from the front, the second in three-quarter view: his face, his short hair, his build and his height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; his clothes here are a dark-green jacket open over a white shirt, dark jeans and brown shoes.

Every object stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. Nothing in the picture carries any writing, numbers or print: the form on the desk is a plain sheet with empty boxes and lines, the papers are blank, the folders on the shelf are plain coloured folders with blank spines, the computer screen is dark, the wall calendar is a plain grid with no numbers, the wall clock has a plain face and no numbers, the passport is a plain dark-red booklet, there is no number display and no sign, no logo and no name plate anywhere.

THE DESK runs across the middle of the picture, a grey laminate desk seen from slightly to the side. On it, from the left of the picture to the right:
- a dark computer screen with a keyboard and a mouse, turned towards the clerk;
- a black telephone;
- a wooden stamp standing on its pad;
- the plain form with empty boxes, lying in front of the young man, with a blue pen in his hand;
- his dark-red passport lying open beside the form;
- a small grey printer at the end of the desk;
- a small green plant in a pot.

THE CLERK, a woman of about fifty-five with short grey hair and glasses, in a blue cardigan over a white blouse, sits behind the desk on an office chair and watches the young man sign, holding a plain white sheet in her hand.

THE YOUNG MAN of the reference pictures sits on a plain black chair in front of the desk, seen from the side and whole from his head to his shoes, which stand on the grey carpet floor. He is caught in the middle of signing the form: the tip of his pen touches the bottom line of the form, his other hand holds the sheet flat, his face concentrated. His black backpack stands on the floor beside his chair.

THE BACK WALL, from the left to the right:
- a white shelf with a row of plain coloured folders standing on it and a stack of white paper;
- a wall calendar with a plain grid and no numbers;
- a round wall clock with a plain white face and no numbers;
- a framed photograph of a lake with trees, in a plain black frame;
- a window with white blinds half open and the grey sky outside;
- a white radiator under the window.

THE RIGHT SIDE of the picture, by the door:
- two grey chairs against the wall, and on one of them a young woman of about thirty with dark curly hair, in a yellow coat, waits with a baby of about one year asleep on her lap;
- a grey waste bin on the floor beside the chairs;
- the white door of the office, closed;
- a tall green plant in a pot in the corner.

THE FRONT of the picture, the lower part: the grey carpet floor, with a desk lamp standing on the corner of the desk nearest to the camera.
